@startuml
title "RAG from Scratch"

rectangle "Document" as document<<Initial document to be processed>>
rectangle "Text" as text<<Parsed text from the document>>
rectangle "Chunks" as chunks<<Text divided into chunks>>
rectangle "Embedding Model" as embeddingModel<<Model to encode text into embeddings>>
rectangle "Embeddings" as embeddings<<Encoded text as embeddings>>
database "PGVector Vector database" as pgvectorVectorDatabase<<Storage for document embeddings>>
actor "User" as user<<Person querying the system>>
rectangle "Query" as query<<User's query>>
rectangle "Embedding" as embedding<<Encoded query as embeddings>>
rectangle "Relevant chunks" as relevantChunks<<Chunks relevant to the query>>
rectangle "User query" as userQuery<<Query from the user>>
rectangle "Prompt (query + context)" as prompt<<Combined query and context>>
rectangle "LLM" as llm<<Large Language Model>>
rectangle "Response" as response<<Generated response>>

document --> text : Parse
text --> chunks : Chunk
chunks --> embeddingModel : Encode
embeddingModel --> embeddings : Encode
embeddings --> pgvectorVectorDatabase : Store
user --> query : Gets
query --> embeddingModel : Encode
embedding --> pgvectorVectorDatabase : Similarity search for relevant chunks
pgvectorVectorDatabase --> relevantChunks : Returns
relevantChunks --> prompt : Combine
userQuery --> prompt : Augment
prompt --> llm : Feed
llm --> response : Generate

legend
- The 'Document' is parsed into 'Text'.
- The 'Text' is divided into 'Chunks'.
- 'Chunks' are encoded by the 'Embedding Model' into 'Embeddings'.
- 'Embeddings' are stored in the 'PGVector Vector database'.
- A 'User' provides a 'Query'.
- The 'Query' is encoded by the 'Embedding model' into 'Embedding'.
- 'Embedding' is used to perform a similarity search in the 'PGVector Vector database' for 'Relevant chunks'.
- 'Relevant chunks' are combined with 'User query' to form a 'Prompt (query + context)'.
- The 'Prompt (query + context)' is fed into the 'LLM'.
- The 'LLM' generates a 'Response'.
end legend
@enduml